.TH simple_shell 1 "August 2025" "Holberton School" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simple_shell \- a simple UNIX command line interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simple_shell
.RI [ no\ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B simple_shell
program is a minimal implementation of a UNIX command line interpreter.

It provides a prompt to the user, waits for input, executes the given command,
and displays the prompt again after execution.

Supported features:
.IP \(bu 2
Displays a prompt (#cisfun$ ) and waits for user input
.IP \(bu 2
Executes a command given as an absolute or relative path
.IP \(bu 2
Handles errors when the command cannot be executed
.IP \(bu 2
Handles the end-of-file (Ctrl+D) condition

Limitations:
.IP \(bu 2
Does not handle command arguments
.IP \(bu 2
Does not use the PATH environment variable to search for executables
.IP \(bu 2
Does not support built-in commands
.IP \(bu 2
Does not support advanced features such as pipes, redirections, or special characters
.SH USAGE
Run the shell:

.EX
$ ./hsh
#cisfun$ /bin/ls
file1 file2 file3
#cisfun$ /bin/pwd
/home/user
#cisfun$ ^D
$
.EE

The shell will execute the command if found; otherwise, it will print an error message.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The shell returns the exit status of the last command executed.
